--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE / APPROACH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web page renders a PageContainer (title + subtitle + page-level loading), a
VehicleSelect + RangePicker action row, an `anyError` AlertBanner
(error.loadFailed), and TWO inline GlassPanels — GlassPanel1 the insecure-alert
(shown when `!isSecure && latest`, body `admin.security.alert`) and GlassPanel2
the digital-twin VehicleTwin panel — followed by the SummaryStatsRow /
SecurityStatusCards / WindowStatusDetail / LiveVehicleState / SentryModeChart /
SecurityStatistics / EventHistoryTable / EventTimeline sub-components (each its
OWN parity unit).

Manifest record for this PAGE unit requires PARITY 9 = 2 panels (GlassPanel1,
GlassPanel2) + 3 states (loading, error, success) + 4 strings
(admin.security.alert, admin.security.subtitle, admin.security.title,
error.loadFailed). This unit ships the routed, adaptive SwiftUI SCREEN that binds
the two data sources (useSecurityEvents → GET /security, useVehicles →
GET /vehicles) through an @Observable model and renders the page chrome, both
GlassPanels, every data state, AND a native rendition of the page's security
sections (live posture, summary, statistics, history, timeline) so the page is
faithful — not a 2-panel stub (Covenant #2/#4/#5). Web i18n key names are reused
verbatim so the section copy matches the web 1:1.

SELF-CONTAINED (house pattern): no page in this repo composes the P4 feature
views; the routed admin pages (SlowQueries, AuditLog, …) are self-contained
Page + PageModel + Models(seam+sample) + RouteRegistration with an injectable
data-source seam (default = local sample; production injects the KMP-backed
AdminStore.securityEvents + vehicles adapter, ADR-004). This unit follows that
exact shape. The native security `SecuritySignal`/`WindowState`/`SecurityMetricTile`
type names already exist in the feature-view module, so the page's own types are
namespaced SecurityAccess*/SecurityPostureTile/SecurityStatItem to avoid the
single-module collision (no redeclaration; confirmed by build).

OUTPUT-PATH DEVIATION (recorded — no silent drift): the generated prompt names
apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/** — a path that does NOT exist in this repo
and that the XcodeGen project.yml does NOT enumerate as a source root, so files
placed there would never compile or test. The real, build-enumerated conventions
are Sources/Features/<Domain>/** (pages) + Tests/Unit/Features/<Domain>/**
(co-located XCTest) — the same roots every accepted sibling P7 admin page used
(SlowQueriesPage, AuditLogPage, …). Files shipped there; all compile into the
single TeslaSync module. Navigation registration touches Sources/App/AppRoute.swift
(+ .securityAccess case) + Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift (registry wiring) — the
"navigation registration" allowed-files clause.

