--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
IMPLEMENTATION (SwiftUI + Apple HIG)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Navigation: AppRoute.securityAccess (pathSegment "security-access" → web
  /security-access resolves canonically via AppRouteParser; group .vehicle —
  the web "Security" sidebar group neighbourhood). SecurityAccessRouteRegistration
  registers the page on the route-host registry, wired in TeslaSyncApp like every
  sibling admin page; deep-link + sidebar reachable.
- Screen scaffold: SecurityAccessPage (SwiftUI View) + @Observable @MainActor
  SecurityAccessPageModel — owns the combined load state of useSecurityEvents +
  useVehicles, the persisted vehicle selection (web useSelectedVehicle), and
  load()/refresh()/selectVehicle()/reload(). No networking/business logic in the
  view (ADR-004); data via the injectable SecurityAccessDataSource seam.
- Adaptive (ADR-002/006): the posture/summary/statistics tiles flow in an
  adaptive LazyVGrid (wide on macOS/iPad, stacked on compact iPhone via
  horizontalSizeClass, #if os gated); navigationBarTitleDisplayMode is iOS-gated.
- GlassPanel1: insecureAlertPanel (TSGlassPanel) renders admin.security.alert in
  danger tone when model.showsInsecureAlert (web `!isSecure && latest`).
- GlassPanel2: SecurityLiveStatePanel (TSGlassPanel) — HIG-native rendition of the
  web VehicleTwin panel: the live lock/sentry/doors/windows posture from `latest`,
  with the web empty fallback admin.security.live.noData (never a blank box).
- 4 data states: loading (TSSkeleton) / empty (ContentUnavailableView via
  TSEmptyState) / error (TSAlertBanner error.loadFailed + TSErrorDisplay retry →
  refresh) / loaded (both panels + summary + statistics + history + timeline). The
  manifest's loading/error/success all render from the bound @Observable model.
- i18n (ADR-014): every visible string via LocalizedStringKey from the catalog;
  web key names preserved; relative time via the localized RelativeDateTimeFormatter.
- a11y (ADR-015): accessibilityElement/.combine + .contain on panels and tiles,
  accessibilityLabel on the selector + section containers, Dynamic Type fonts
  (Font.TS), light/dark via the design tokens, ≥44pt menu targets.
- Units (ADR-005): N/A — security state is booleans / enum strings / timestamps;
  no SI quantities. Sentry uptime is a ratio %; counts are unit-agnostic.

